% SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
% =====================================================================
% queries.clausal -- QUERY-COMBINATOR layer for ind/dpdp_notice_consent.
% A TOP-LAYER consumer: it imports the determination slice's PUBLIC
% predicates it calls, and nothing else.
%
% Query types this domain serves:
%   #2 eligibility    decide_dpdp_notice_consent/2 and
%                     dpdp_notice_consent_status/2 (in the slice): eligible,
%                     ineligible or indeterminate for the consent ground of
%                     s 4(1)(a), mapped from consent_ground/3.
%   #7 justification  dpdp_notice_consent_checklist/2 (in the slice): one
%                     item(RequirementId, Status, cite(Key)) row per condition.
%   #16 what-if       dpdp_notice_consent_what_if/4 (here): one key
%                     overridden, the facade status re-evaluated. The
%                     profile is an ATTRIBUTE LIST, not a dict, so the kit's
%                     dict-based override_key/4 does not apply: the override
%                     is written here for attribute lists.
% The six contract queries (consent_ground/3, legitimate_use_ground/3,
% consent_notice/3, withdrawal_effect/3, consent_manager_status/3,
% provision_lists/2) are exported by the slice itself; the input check
% dpdp_notice_consent_input_problems/2 is re-exported here as the scaffold
% wrote it in the kernel.
%
% ROOT EXPORTS. The scorer reads the profile key atoms, the judgement value
% unsure, the enumeration value atoms, the topic atoms, the content item
% atoms and the result atoms as package-root attributes, and the result
% constructors (indeterminate/1, needs_legal_review/2, open_textured/2,
% inputs_relied_on/1, content_item/2, input_problems/1, unknown_key/1,
% wrong_type/1, duplicate_key/1, date/3) with them. The atoms are defined
% here as facts; the constructors are DATA, declared with constructors/1 and
% given no clauses, except date/3, the input date form of question_date,
% which holds for a date(Year, Month, Day) of three integers. None decides a
% statutory condition.
%
% provenance/2: provenance(CitationKey, PinnedUnit) relates a recorded
% citation key to the pinned unit it cites (the ref of its citation/2
% record); the optional provenance context item of needs_legal_review/2
% carries the same pair.
%
% Nothing here decides a statutory condition: no implements/1 marker.
% =====================================================================

:- module(queries, [
    dpdp_notice_consent_profile_keys/1,
    dpdp_notice_consent_input_problems/2,
    dpdp_notice_consent_what_if/4,
    provenance/2,
    sections_4_to_7_in_force/0,
    section_6_9_in_force/0,
    question_date/0,
    acts_as_data_fiduciary/0,
    lawful_purpose/0,
    consent_given/0,
    consent_withdrawn/0,
    consent_meets_section_6_1/0,
